  (1, 'AF-000001', 'Minister Lana Popham provided an update relevant to North Coast (Prince Rupert, Haida Gwaii), wit...', 2, NULL, 'TWO-DAY GATHERING: Minister Lana Popham provided an update relevant to North Coast (Prince Rupert, Haida Gwaii), with initiatives connected to the AF mandate and partners like BC Milk Marketing Board, Investment Agriculture Foundation, BC Farmers'' Markets. Regional stakeholders from North Coast (Prince Rupert, Haida Gwaii) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'In practical terms: It supports local hiring and keeps dollars circulating here. Less red tape and more coordination make it easier to plan ahead. More predictability; better service; safer communities.', true, false, '2027-03-03', '2027-03-03', 2, '10:45:00', '11:45:00', 2, 'Targeting late Q1; coordinating venues with local partners. Media advisory to follow.', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Two-day gathering: Minister Lana Popham summarized AF actions in North Coast (Prince Rupert, Haida Gwaii), with partners like BC Milk Marketing Board. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 3, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 2, 9, 3, 1, 1, '2025-12-08 23:06:43-08', '2026-02-18 08:15:14-08', 1),
  (2, 'AG-000002', 'Attorney General Niki Sharma introduced measures to streamline the Civil Resolution Tribunal and ...', 3, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Attorney General Niki Sharma introduced measures to streamline the Civil Resolution Tribunal and bolster resources for the BC Prosecution Service, reducing delays while improving victim services coordination in Columbia-Shuswap. Reforms include digital filing pilots and cross-agency protocols with public safety partners to tackle repeat violent offending. Regional stakeholders from Columbia-Shuswap will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Short version: Streamlined tribunals and prosecutions mean faster resolutions for victims and businesses–less time lost to paperwork. Digital filing and data–sharing cut backlogs so serious cases move quicker. More predictability; better service; safer communities.', false, false, '2027-04-01', '2027-04-01', 2, '10:30:00', '13:30:00', 2, 'Week of next full moon–exact date pending room availability in community hall.', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Niki Sharma summarized AG actions in Columbia-Shuswap, with partners like BC Prosecution Service. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 3, 10, 3, 1, 1, '2026-01-14 02:13:14-08', '2026-01-30 18:27:02-08', 1),
  (3, 'MCFD-000003', 'Minister Jodie Wickens announced expanded supports for youth in care and children and youth with ...', 4, NULL, 'COMMUNITY ROUNDTABLE: Minister Jodie Wickens announced expanded supports for youth in care and children and youth with support needs in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky, co-designed with Indigenous partners and community agencies. The initiative strengthens culturally safe services and transitions to adulthood with housing and education pathways. Regional stakeholders from Whistler and Sea-to-Sky will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Why people care: Expanded CYWSN and youth–in–care supports close service gaps and ease transitions to housing, work and school. Less paperwork, clearer timelines, fewer surprises.', false, false, '2027-03-18', '2027-03-18', 2, '12:30:00', '13:30:00', 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, 'Community roundtable: Minister Jodie Wickens summarized CFD actions in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky, with partners like BCGEU. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', true, NULL, NULL, 1, 3, NULL, NULL, 'team', 4, 11, 5, 1, 1, '2025-02-23 17:26:14-08', '2026-02-18 06:45:41-08', 1),
  (4, 'CITZ-000004', 'Minister Diana Gibson announced a digital service refresh for Service BC locations in Skeena (Ter...', 5, NULL, 'STAKEHOLDER CALL: Minister Diana Gibson announced a digital service refresh for Service BC locations in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), expanding identity verification, permitting portals and connectivity with the BCDevExchange community. The work advances secure-by-design standards and plain-language service improvements across channels. Regional stakeholders from Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'What changes on the ground: Service BC upgrades reduce lineups–more done online, fewer repeat visits. Plain–language, secure–by–design services make government simpler and safer to use. It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns.', false, false, '2027-04-29', '2027-04-29', 1, '16:30:00', '17:00:00', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Stakeholder call: Minister Diana Gibson summarized CITZ actions in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), with partners like BC Registries. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', true, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 5, 12, 3, 1, 1, '2025-11-25 22:27:21-08', '2026-02-15 00:48:51-08', 1),
  (5, 'ECC-000005', 'Minister Lisa Beare outlined new classroom additions and early learning spaces in Saanich Peninsu...', 6, NULL, 'REGIONAL TOUR STOP: Minister Lisa Beare outlined new classroom additions and early learning spaces in Saanich Peninsula, coordinated with school districts and BCTF to support enrolment growth and workforce needs. Funding also supports seismic upgrades and inclusive education resources developed with local educators. Regional stakeholders from Saanich Peninsula will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Bottom line– Better supports for inclusive education mean more kids can thrive close to home. More predictability; better service; safer communities.', false, false, '2027-01-28', '2027-01-28', 2, '09:00:00', '11:00:00', 2, 'Tentative: first week of next month, subject to travel windows and weather.', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Regional tour stop: Minister Lisa Beare summarized ECC actions in Saanich Peninsula, with partners like BC School Trustees Association. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 6, 13, 3, 1, 1, '2025-01-26 10:06:05-08', '2026-02-21 00:20:43-08', 1),
  (6, 'EMCR-000006', 'Minister Kelly Greene detailed seasonal preparedness for floods, drought and wildfire in Victoria...', 7, NULL, 'MEDIA AVAIL: Minister Kelly Greene detailed seasonal preparedness for floods, drought and wildfire in Victoria, highlighting resources from PreparedBC and EmergencyInfoBC and community-level evacuation planning. Investments include modernized emergency operations centres and enhanced public alerting with local authorities. Regional stakeholders from Victoria will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'For locals: Co–ordinated planning reduces overlap and confusion between agencies on bad days. Better alerts, evacuation routes and EOC capacity in Victoria save lives when floods or fires strike. It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns.', true, true, '2027-02-01', '2027-02-01', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Media avail: Minister Kelly Greene summarized EMCR actions in Victoria, with partners like BC Wildfire Service. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'issues', true, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 7, 14, 4, 1, 1, '2024-12-26 01:46:29-08', '2026-02-13 11:38:16-08', 1),
  (7, 'ECS-000007', 'Minister Adrian Dix outlined grid-scale investments with BC Hydro and industrial electrification ...', 8, NULL, 'THIRD-PARTY EVENT: Minister Adrian Dix outlined grid-scale investments with BC Hydro and industrial electrification opportunities in Sunshine Coast, advancing CleanBC goals and supporting new critical-minerals processing. The plan includes fast-tracked interconnections for future projects and expanded heat-pump incentives for homes and small businesses. Regional stakeholders from Sunshine Coast will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Faster interconnections mean clean projects come online sooner, reducing energy costs over time. Heat–pump incentives lower household bills and improve comfort during heat waves and cold snaps. That means time back in people’s days and money kept in local pockets.', false, false, '2027-02-12', '2027-02-12', 1, '11:45:00', '12:45:00', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Third-party event: Minister Adrian Dix summarized ECS actions in Sunshine Coast, with partners like BC Hydro. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 8, 15, 3, 1, 1, '2024-12-27 20:39:56-08', '2025-03-13 12:05:35-08', 1),
  (8, 'EP-000008', 'Minister Tamara Davidson announced expanded conservation investments and trail upgrades in Prince...', 9, NULL, 'MEDIA AVAIL: Minister Tamara Davidson announced expanded conservation investments and trail upgrades in Prince George, with BC Parks and the Conservation Officer Service enhancing access while supporting habitat and climate resilience. The ministry also highlighted permitting efficiencies through the Environmental Assessment Office for clean-economy projects. Regional stakeholders from Prince George will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'In practical terms: Upgraded trails and habitat work in Prince George balance access and conservation–good for residents, tourism and wildlife. The changes are small on paper but add up across a year of errands, commitments and bills. That means time back in people’s days and money kept in local pockets.', false, false, '2027-12-19', '2027-12-19', 1, '14:00:00', '15:00:00', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Media avail: Minister Tamara Davidson summarized EP actions in Prince George, with partners like BC Parks. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 9, 16, 3, 1, 1, '2025-02-20 07:49:18-08', '2026-01-25 22:04:02-08', 1),
  (9, 'FIN-000009', 'Minister Brenda Bailey previewed fiscal guardrails and targeted affordability measures, noting on...', 10, NULL, 'STAKEHOLDER CALL: Minister Brenda Bailey previewed fiscal guardrails and targeted affordability measures, noting ongoing coordination with BC Assessment and InBC to support productivity and jobs across Sunshine Coast amid tariff volatility. Measures include focused relief for low- and fixed-income households and disciplined capital planning to protect core services. Regional stakeholders from Sunshine Coast will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Targeted relief cushions households from rising costs while keeping capital projects moving–protecting services people rely on. Backing productivity and small–business cashflow helps communities ride out tariffs without losing local jobs. That means time back in people’s days and money kept in local pockets.', false, false, '2026-12-01', '2026-12-01', 1, '10:00:00', '13:00:00', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Stakeholder call: Minister Brenda Bailey summarized FIN actions in Sunshine Coast, with partners like BC Lottery Corporation. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 3, NULL, NULL, 'team', 10, 17, 3, 1, 1, '2025-01-24 20:53:23-08', '2025-09-14 03:24:17-08', 1),
  (10, 'FOR-000010', 'Minister Ravi Parmar discussed wildfire readiness and fibre supply certainty in North Shore, incl...', 11, NULL, 'THIRD-PARTY EVENT: Minister Ravi Parmar discussed wildfire readiness and fibre supply certainty in North Shore, including community resilience projects and partnerships with First Nations and BC Timber Sales. The briefing addressed support for affected workers, value-added manufacturing, and steps to accelerate reforestation. Regional stakeholders from North Shore will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'If you live here: Support for value–added manufacturing diversifies jobs beyond log exports. Wildfire readiness and fibre–supply clarity help mills plan shifts and keep crews working in North Shore. It supports local hiring and keeps dollars circulating here.', false, false, '2026-12-04', '2026-12-04', 2, '13:00:00', '14:00:00', 2, 'Rolling announcement series; this stop follows Prince George and precedes Kelowna.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Third-party event: Minister Ravi Parmar summarized FOR actions in North Shore, with partners like BC Timber Sales. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 11, 18, 3, 1, 1, '2025-03-15 08:44:59-08', '2026-02-22 23:22:15-08', 1),
  (11, 'HLTH-000011', 'Minister Josie Osborne provided an update on primary care access and ER stabilization in Cariboo ...', 12, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Minister Josie Osborne provided an update on primary care access and ER stabilization in Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel), highlighting new Urgent and Primary Care Centre hours and Island-wide recruitment initiatives with health authorities like Island Health. The announcement also referenced ongoing work to integrate mental-health and addictions services within the broader care system. Regional stakeholders from Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'For families: More predictable clinic hours and integrated mental–health supports mean people get help sooner, not just at crisis points. Recruitment wins translate to fewer closures and shorter distances to care for rural patients. People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days.', false, false, '2027-06-26', '2027-06-26', 2, '11:15:00', '12:15:00', 2, 'Targeting late Q1; coordinating venues with local partners. Media advisory to follow.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Josie Osborne summarized HLTH actions in Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel), with partners like PHSA. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 12, 19, 6, 1, 1, '2025-02-09 07:10:29-08', '2026-02-18 20:10:34-08', 1),
  (12, 'HMA-000012', 'Minister Christine Boyle confirmed additional BC Builds sites and transit-oriented development pa...', 13, NULL, 'COMMUNITY ROUNDTABLE: Minister Christine Boyle confirmed additional BC Builds sites and transit-oriented development partnerships in Boundary Country, advancing gentle density reforms under the MUNI file with local governments. Work with BC Housing and the BC Rent Bank network will target rental supply, student housing, and non-market homes aligned to community plans. Regional stakeholders from Boundary Country will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'For businesses: Clear rules reduce rezoning fights and speed up permits so homes show up years, not decades, sooner. BC Builds sites bring predictable delivery and more non–market options–stability for families, students, and seniors on fixed incomes.', false, false, '2027-05-10', '2027-05-10', 2, '14:00:00', '15:00:00', 2, 'Tentative: first week of next month, subject to travel windows and weather.', NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, 'Community roundtable: Minister Christine Boyle summarized HMA actions in Boundary Country, with partners like BC Housing. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 13, 20, 3, 1, 1, '2024-12-07 21:20:53-08', '2025-02-02 20:44:35-08', 1),
  (13, 'IRR-000013', 'Minister Spencer Chandra Herbert provided an update relevant to Surrey-Delta, with initiatives co...', 14, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Minister Spencer Chandra Herbert provided an update relevant to Surrey-Delta, with initiatives connected to the IRR mandate and partners like First Nations Leadership Council, Council of the Haida Nation, UBCM. Regional stakeholders from Surrey-Delta will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting. Engagement will continue through webinars and in-person sessions to refine delivery details before rollout.', 'The changes are small on paper but add up across a year of errands, commitments and bills. The changes are small on paper but add up across a year of errands, commitments and bills. It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns.', false, false, '2027-09-10', '2027-09-10', 3, '14:45:00', '17:45:00', 3, 'Pushing back one week to sync with email campaign timeline; MO approved, date unconfirmed.', NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Spencer Chandra Herbert summarized IRR actions in Surrey-Delta, with partners like First Nations Leadership Council. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 14, 21, 3, 1, 1, '2025-07-27 08:04:13-08', '2026-02-18 01:51:20-08', 1),
  (14, 'INF-000014', 'Minister Bowinn Ma described delivery timelines for community and health capital projects in Suns...', 15, NULL, 'PHOTO-OP & MINISTRY NR: Minister Bowinn Ma described delivery timelines for community and health capital projects in Sunshine Coast, leveraging benefits agreements and BC Infrastructure Benefits to maximize local hiring. Projects will incorporate low-carbon construction materials and climate resilience standards. Regional stakeholders from Sunshine Coast will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'From a resident’s view: On–time capital builds mean local jobs now and modern hospitals, schools and community hubs later in Sunshine Coast. Community benefits agreements create apprenticeships close to home. It’s incremental, but tangible.', false, false, '2027-12-19', '2027-12-19', 2, '16:45:00', '17:00:00', 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, 'Photo-op & ministry nr: Minister Bowinn Ma summarized INF actions in Sunshine Coast, with partners like Transportation Investment Corporation. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 15, 22, 4, 1, 1, '2025-02-24 15:25:56-08', '2026-01-26 22:20:13-08', 1),
  (15, 'JEG-000015', 'Minister Ravi Kahlon highlighted new trade diversification projects and a talent strategy for cle...', 17, NULL, 'FYI ONLY: Minister Ravi Kahlon highlighted new trade diversification projects and a talent strategy for clean tech and life sciences in Saanich Peninsula, delivered with Innovate BC and partners through Look West. The update included targeted supports for SMEs, export-readiness training, and investment attraction for anchor employers. Regional stakeholders from Saanich Peninsula will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Why people care: Trade diversification and anchor investments bring steady work to Saanich Peninsula suppliers, not just big centres. SME supports (exports, productivity, hiring) help firms keep people on during uncertainty. It’s incremental, but tangible.', false, true, '2027-05-06', '2027-05-06', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Fyi only: Minister Ravi Kahlon summarized JEDI actions in Saanich Peninsula, with partners like Innovate BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 3, NULL, NULL, 'global', 17, 24, 3, 1, 1, '2025-01-21 17:34:16-08', '2026-02-07 08:08:15-08', 1),
  (16, 'LAB-000016', 'Minister Jennifer Whiteside announced worker-safety initiatives and updates to employment standar...', 18, NULL, 'PHOTO-OP & MINISTRY NR: Minister Jennifer Whiteside announced worker-safety initiatives and updates to employment standards affecting Richmond, in partnership with WorkSafeBC and labour stakeholders. The package includes protections for gig workers, anti-harassment measures and multilingual employer outreach. Regional stakeholders from Richmond will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Anti–harassment measures and multilingual outreach make rights real on the shop floor. Clearer standards reduce disputes and level the playing field.', true, false, '2027-07-05', '2027-07-05', 2, '13:45:00', '15:45:00', 2, 'Morning event preferred; avoid municipal budget deliberations week.', NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, 'Photo-op & ministry nr: Minister Jennifer Whiteside summarized LAB actions in Richmond, with partners like WorkSafeBC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 18, 25, 6, 1, 1, '2025-10-20 04:32:31-08', '2026-02-10 18:25:23-08', 1),
  (17, 'MIN-000017', 'Minister Jagrup Brar provided an update on critical-minerals roadmaps and permitting in Sooke and...', 19, NULL, 'MEDIA AVAIL: Minister Jagrup Brar provided an update on critical-minerals roadmaps and permitting in Sooke and West Shore, aligning power access with BC Hydro and workforce partnerships for responsible development. The strategy advances downstream processing and Indigenous participation benefits agreements. Regional stakeholders from Sooke and West Shore will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Responsible permitting and power access let projects advance while protecting water and local values. Benefit agreements with Nations build durable partnerships. People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days. It supports local hiring and keeps dollars circulating here.', true, true, '2026-12-27', '2026-12-27', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Rolling announcement series; this stop follows Prince George and precedes Kelowna.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Media avail: Minister Jagrup Brar summarized MIN actions in Sooke and West Shore, with partners like Geoscience BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 19, 26, 3, 1, 1, '2025-12-23 04:40:10-08', '2026-02-18 15:49:51-08', 1),
  (18, 'PSFS-000018', 'Minister Jessie Sunner highlighted micro-credentials and co-op expansions in East Kootenay (Cranb...', 20, NULL, 'TWO-DAY GATHERING: Minister Jessie Sunner highlighted micro-credentials and co-op expansions in East Kootenay (Cranbrook, Fernie), supported by StudentAid BC and EducationPlannerBC, to align learners with high-demand jobs in tech, health and trades. New student housing and skills grants will reduce barriers for rural and Indigenous learners. Regional stakeholders from East Kootenay (Cranbrook, Fernie) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Community impact: Micro–credentials and co–ops align programs with real jobs; grads stay in East Kootenay (Cranbrook, Fernie). New student beds free up rental stock and shorten commutes. That means time back in people’s days and money kept in local pockets.', false, false, '2027-03-09', '2027-03-09', 2, '15:15:00', '16:15:00', 2, 'Tentative: first week of next month, subject to travel windows and weather.', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Two-day gathering: Minister Jessie Sunner summarized PSFS actions in East Kootenay (Cranbrook, Fernie), with partners like StudentAid BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 20, 27, 4, 1, 1, '2025-04-10 14:33:16-08', '2026-02-10 02:24:24-08', 1),
  (19, 'PSSG-000019', 'Minister Garry Begg announced expanded enforcement against organized crime and retail theft, coor...', 21, NULL, 'BUDGET BACKGROUNDER: Minister Garry Begg announced expanded enforcement against organized crime and retail theft, coordinated with BC RCMP and municipal police in Saanich Peninsula and supported by modernized information sharing. The program includes investments in community safety teams and better supports for victims and small businesses. Regional stakeholders from Saanich Peninsula will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'More support for victims reduces re–traumatization and improves reporting. It nudges long–term resilience, not just short–term fixes.', false, false, '2027-05-13', '2027-05-13', 2, '16:45:00', '17:00:00', 2, 'Morning event preferred; avoid municipal budget deliberations week.', NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, 'Budget backgrounder: Minister Garry Begg summarized PSSG actions in Saanich Peninsula, with partners like BC RCMP. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 3, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 21, 28, 4, 1, 1, '2025-07-11 21:56:34-08', '2025-09-08 00:43:46-08', 1),
  (20, 'SDPR-000020', 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Sheila Malcolmson announced improvements to disability assistance and employ...', 22, NULL, 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Sheila Malcolmson announced improvements to disability assistance and employment services in Esquimalt, coordinated through WorkBC and community partners to reduce barriers. The update included simplified applications, earnings exemptions and culturally responsive supports. Regional stakeholders from Esquimalt will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Why people care: Culturally responsive services meet people where they are, not the other way around. It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns.', true, false, '2027-04-20', '2027-04-20', 2, '16:45:00', '17:45:00', 2, 'Embargoed until 09:00 PT on release day. Virtual technical briefing the day before.', NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, 'Open house: Minister Sheila Malcolmson summarized SDPR actions in Esquimalt, with partners like Service BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 22, 29, 3, 1, 1, '2025-04-13 05:29:00-08', '2025-11-22 10:07:18-08', 1),
  (21, 'TACS-000021', 'Minister Anne Kang announced destination development funding, film incentives and sport event sup...', 23, NULL, 'THIRD-PARTY EVENT: Minister Anne Kang announced destination development funding, film incentives and sport event support in Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel), working with Destination BC and Creative BC to extend shoulder-season visits. Investments will improve accessibility, trail networks and cultural spaces in collaboration with local nations. Regional stakeholders from Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'If you live here: Destination upgrades and film incentives smooth out shoulder seasons–stable hours for hospitality workers in Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel). People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days. Less paperwork, clearer timelines, fewer surprises.', false, false, '2027-06-18', '2027-06-18', 2, '12:30:00', '13:30:00', 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Third-party event: Minister Anne Kang summarized TACS actions in Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel), with partners like Destination BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 3, NULL, NULL, 'global', 23, 30, 3, 1, 1, '2025-05-22 16:58:06-08', '2025-08-22 08:32:48-08', 1),
  (22, 'MOTT-000022', 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Mike Farnworth outlined near-term upgrades to Highway 1 and transit hubs, in...', 24, NULL, 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Mike Farnworth outlined near-term upgrades to Highway 1 and transit hubs, including new bus priority lanes in Victoria, while continuing work with TransLink and BC Transit on ridership recovery and with BC Ferries on sailing reliability. The update included construction milestones for active transportation links and integrated fare pilots to simplify inter-regional travel. Regional stakeholders from Victoria will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Why it matters: Safer corridors and active–transportation links open school and work options for people who don’t drive, cutting emissions with everyday trips. Victoria commuters get faster, more reliable trips–bus lanes and integrated fares mean fewer missed connections and less time in traffic.', false, false, '2027-02-16', '2027-02-16', 2, '12:00:00', '15:00:00', 2, 'Week of next full moon–exact date pending room availability in community hall.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Open house: Minister Mike Farnworth summarized MOTI actions in Victoria, with partners like TransLink. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation. The update aligns with government priorities and reinforces collaboration across ministries and Indigenous partners.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 24, 31, 3, 1, 1, '2025-11-05 04:23:48-08', '2026-02-15 20:32:38-08', 1),
  (23, 'WLRS-000023', 'Minister Randene Neill outlined watershed security actions in Boundary Country, integrating habit...', 25, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Minister Randene Neill outlined watershed security actions in Boundary Country, integrating habitat restoration with Living Lakes Canada and expanded data-sharing to support permitting and drought response. The plan strengthens cumulative effects management and inter-ministry coordination. Regional stakeholders from Boundary Country will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Watershed security and drought planning protect drinking water and farms in Boundary Country. Better data and permitting clarity speed up habitat fixes. The changes are small on paper but add up across a year of errands, commitments and bills.', false, true, '2027-04-03', '2027-04-03', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Randene Neill summarized WLRS actions in Boundary Country, with partners like BC Parks. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 25, 32, 3, 1, 1, '2024-11-15 16:58:00-08', '2026-03-03 08:22:33-08', 1),
  (24, 'AF-000024', 'Minister Lana Popham provided an update relevant to Langley, with initiatives connected to the AF...', 2, NULL, 'THIRD-PARTY EVENT: Minister Lana Popham provided an update relevant to Langley, with initiatives connected to the AF mandate and partners like BC Milk Marketing Board, Investment Agriculture Foundation, BC Farmers'' Markets. Regional stakeholders from Langley will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting. Engagement will continue through webinars and in-person sessions to refine delivery details before rollout.', 'It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns. The changes are small on paper but add up across a year of errands, commitments and bills. That means time back in people’s days and money kept in local pockets.', false, true, '2027-04-07', '2027-04-07', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Third-party event: Minister Lana Popham summarized AF actions in Langley, with partners like BC Milk Marketing Board. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 2, 9, 3, 1, 1, '2024-11-12 09:15:03-08', '2026-02-05 03:59:23-08', 1),
  (25, 'AG-000025', 'Attorney General Niki Sharma introduced measures to streamline the Civil Resolution Tribunal and ...', 3, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Attorney General Niki Sharma introduced measures to streamline the Civil Resolution Tribunal and bolster resources for the BC Prosecution Service, reducing delays while improving victim services coordination in Burnaby-New Westminster. Reforms include digital filing pilots and cross-agency protocols with public safety partners to tackle repeat violent offending. Regional stakeholders from Burnaby-New Westminster will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Bottom line– Clearer pathways help people self–resolve disputes without costly court time. Less red tape and more coordination make it easier to plan ahead. Less paperwork, clearer timelines, fewer surprises.', false, false, '2027-03-31', '2027-03-31', 2, '15:00:00', '17:00:00', 2, 'Rolling announcement series; this stop follows Prince George and precedes Kelowna.', NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Niki Sharma summarized AG actions in Burnaby-New Westminster, with partners like BC Prosecution Service. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 3, 10, 3, 1, 1, '2026-01-15 02:46:31-08', '2026-02-25 22:37:54-08', 1),
  (26, 'MCFD-000026', 'Minister Jodie Wickens announced expanded supports for youth in care and children and youth with ...', 4, NULL, 'PHOTO-OP & MINISTRY NR: Minister Jodie Wickens announced expanded supports for youth in care and children and youth with support needs in North Coast (Prince Rupert, Haida Gwaii), co-designed with Indigenous partners and community agencies. The initiative strengthens culturally safe services and transitions to adulthood with housing and education pathways. Regional stakeholders from North Coast (Prince Rupert, Haida Gwaii) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Short version: Stability for caregivers and better navigation reduce crisis cycling. Expanded CYWSN and youth–in–care supports close service gaps and ease transitions to housing, work and school. It nudges long–term resilience, not just short–term fixes.', false, false, '2027-04-10', '2027-04-10', 3, '16:15:00', '17:00:00', 3, 'Pushing back one week to sync with email campaign timeline; MO approved, date unconfirmed.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Photo-op & ministry nr: Minister Jodie Wickens summarized CFD actions in North Coast (Prince Rupert, Haida Gwaii), with partners like BCGEU. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 3, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 4, 11, 3, 1, 1, '2025-01-28 21:30:35-08', '2025-03-02 17:49:08-08', 1),
  (27, 'CITZ-000027', 'Minister Diana Gibson announced a digital service refresh for Service BC locations in Richmond, e...', 5, NULL, 'PHOTO-OP & MINISTRY NR: Minister Diana Gibson announced a digital service refresh for Service BC locations in Richmond, expanding identity verification, permitting portals and connectivity with the BCDevExchange community. The work advances secure-by-design standards and plain-language service improvements across channels. Regional stakeholders from Richmond will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Identity and permitting improvements mean faster turnaround for everyday needs (licences, filings, payments).', false, false, '2026-12-27', '2026-12-27', 2, '15:45:00', '17:00:00', 2, 'Week of next full moon–exact date pending room availability in community hall.', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Photo-op & ministry nr: Minister Diana Gibson summarized CITZ actions in Richmond, with partners like BC Registries. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 3, NULL, NULL, 'global', 5, 12, 3, 1, 1, '2025-04-20 13:13:59-08', '2026-02-25 09:17:54-08', 1),
  (28, 'ECC-000028', 'Minister Lisa Beare outlined new classroom additions and early learning spaces in Skeena (Terrace...', 6, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Minister Lisa Beare outlined new classroom additions and early learning spaces in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), coordinated with school districts and BCTF to support enrolment growth and workforce needs. Funding also supports seismic upgrades and inclusive education resources developed with local educators. Regional stakeholders from Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'For locals: Better supports for inclusive education mean more kids can thrive close to home. People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days. It supports local hiring and keeps dollars circulating here.', true, true, '2027-05-23', '2027-05-23', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Lisa Beare summarized ECC actions in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), with partners like BC School Trustees Association. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 6, 13, 3, 1, 1, '2025-05-21 21:41:23-08', '2025-12-12 06:45:19-08', 1),
  (29, 'EMCR-000029', 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Kelly Greene detailed seasonal preparedness for floods, drought and wildfire...', 7, NULL, 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Kelly Greene detailed seasonal preparedness for floods, drought and wildfire in Prince George, highlighting resources from PreparedBC and EmergencyInfoBC and community-level evacuation planning. Investments include modernized emergency operations centres and enhanced public alerting with local authorities. Regional stakeholders from Prince George will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Better alerts, evacuation routes and EOC capacity in Prince George save lives when floods or fires strike.', false, false, '2027-05-22', '2027-05-22', 3, '12:45:00', '15:45:00', 3, 'Pushing back one week to sync with email campaign timeline; MO approved, date unconfirmed.', NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Open house: Minister Kelly Greene summarized EMCR actions in Prince George, with partners like BC Wildfire Service. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 7, 14, 3, 1, 1, '2025-12-31 10:01:37-08', '2026-02-02 03:15:14-08', 1),
  (30, 'ECS-000030', 'Minister Adrian Dix outlined grid-scale investments with BC Hydro and industrial electrification ...', 8, NULL, 'STAKEHOLDER CALL: Minister Adrian Dix outlined grid-scale investments with BC Hydro and industrial electrification opportunities in East Kootenay (Cranbrook, Fernie), advancing CleanBC goals and supporting new critical-minerals processing. The plan includes fast-tracked interconnections for future projects and expanded heat-pump incentives for homes and small businesses. Regional stakeholders from East Kootenay (Cranbrook, Fernie) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Short version: Heat–pump incentives lower household bills and improve comfort during heat waves and cold snaps. Grid upgrades and electrification cut industrial emissions and create skilled jobs in East Kootenay (Cranbrook, Fernie).', false, true, '2027-05-23', '2027-05-23', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Week of next full moon–exact date pending room availability in community hall.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Stakeholder call: Minister Adrian Dix summarized ECS actions in East Kootenay (Cranbrook, Fernie), with partners like BC Hydro. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 8, 15, 4, 1, 1, '2025-03-05 01:14:04-08', '2026-01-23 00:04:45-08', 1),
  (31, 'EP-000031', 'TECHNICAL BRIEFING: Minister Tamara Davidson announced expanded conservation investments and trai...', 9, NULL, 'TECHNICAL BRIEFING: Minister Tamara Davidson announced expanded conservation investments and trail upgrades in Cowichan Valley, with BC Parks and the Conservation Officer Service enhancing access while supporting habitat and climate resilience. The ministry also highlighted permitting efficiencies through the Environmental Assessment Office for clean-economy projects. Regional stakeholders from Cowichan Valley will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'For locals: Cleaner permitting for clean–economy projects pairs jobs with better environmental outcomes.', false, false, '2026-12-24', '2026-12-24', 2, '11:30:00', '13:30:00', 2, 'Tentative: first week of next month, subject to travel windows and weather.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Technical briefing: Minister Tamara Davidson summarized EP actions in Cowichan Valley, with partners like BC Parks. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 9, 16, 3, 1, 1, '2025-04-20 21:31:13-08', '2025-09-10 02:32:15-08', 1),
  (32, 'FIN-000032', 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Brenda Bailey previewed fiscal guardrails and targeted affordability measure...', 10, NULL, 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Brenda Bailey previewed fiscal guardrails and targeted affordability measures, noting ongoing coordination with BC Assessment and InBC to support productivity and jobs across Fraser Valley amid tariff volatility. Measures include focused relief for low- and fixed-income households and disciplined capital planning to protect core services. Regional stakeholders from Fraser Valley will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Fiscal guardrails matter: they reduce risk of sudden cuts to hospitals, schools and transit when volatility hits. People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days. It’s incremental, but tangible.', false, false, '2027-04-02', '2027-04-02', 1, '10:15:00', '11:15:00', 1, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Open house: Minister Brenda Bailey summarized FIN actions in Fraser Valley, with partners like BC Lottery Corporation. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 10, 17, 4, 1, 1, '2025-08-12 15:51:26-08', '2025-12-15 18:36:30-08', 1),
  (33, 'FOR-000033', 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Ravi Parmar discussed wildfire readiness and fibre supply certainty in Whist...', 11, NULL, 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Ravi Parmar discussed wildfire readiness and fibre supply certainty in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky, including community resilience projects and partnerships with First Nations and BC Timber Sales. The briefing addressed support for affected workers, value-added manufacturing, and steps to accelerate reforestation. Regional stakeholders from Whistler and Sea-to-Sky will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'If you live here: Support for value–added manufacturing diversifies jobs beyond log exports. It nudges long–term resilience, not just short–term fixes.', false, false, '2027-01-30', '2027-01-30', 2, '12:00:00', '13:00:00', 2, 'Embargoed until 09:00 PT on release day. Virtual technical briefing the day before.', NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Open house: Minister Ravi Parmar summarized FOR actions in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky, with partners like BC Timber Sales. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 3, NULL, NULL, 'team', 11, 18, 1, 1, 1, '2025-07-13 11:27:26-08', '2026-02-19 08:34:07-08', 1),
  (34, 'HLTH-000034', 'Minister Josie Osborne provided an update on primary care access and ER stabilization in Esquimal...', 12, NULL, 'MEDIA AVAIL: Minister Josie Osborne provided an update on primary care access and ER stabilization in Esquimalt, highlighting new Urgent and Primary Care Centre hours and Island-wide recruitment initiatives with health authorities like Island Health. The announcement also referenced ongoing work to integrate mental-health and addictions services within the broader care system. Regional stakeholders from Esquimalt will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'For businesses: Recruitment wins translate to fewer closures and shorter distances to care for rural patients. Stabilizing ERs and primary care in Esquimalt reduces long waits and expensive out–of–town travel, especially for seniors and families with kids.', false, true, '2027-03-25', '2027-03-25', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Week of next full moon–exact date pending room availability in community hall.', NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, 'Media avail: Minister Josie Osborne summarized HLTH actions in Esquimalt, with partners like PHSA. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation. The update aligns with government priorities and reinforces collaboration across ministries and Indigenous partners.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 12, 19, 3, 1, 1, '2025-10-22 01:25:46-08', '2025-12-12 21:41:41-08', 1),
  (35, 'HMA-000035', 'Minister Christine Boyle confirmed additional BC Builds sites and transit-oriented development pa...', 13, NULL, 'MEDIA AVAIL: Minister Christine Boyle confirmed additional BC Builds sites and transit-oriented development partnerships in Esquimalt, advancing gentle density reforms under the MUNI file with local governments. Work with BC Housing and the BC Rent Bank network will target rental supply, student housing, and non-market homes aligned to community plans. Regional stakeholders from Esquimalt will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Fast–tracked rentals and gentle density near transit in Esquimalt chip away at waitlists and let workers live closer to jobs. BC Builds sites bring predictable delivery and more non–market options–stability for families, students, and seniors on fixed incomes. It supports local hiring and keeps dollars circulating here.', false, false, '2027-05-31', '2027-05-31', 2, '13:45:00', '16:45:00', 2, 'Embargoed until 09:00 PT on release day. Virtual technical briefing the day before.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Media avail: Minister Christine Boyle summarized HMA actions in Esquimalt, with partners like BC Housing. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', true, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 13, 20, 3, 1, 1, '2024-12-06 14:08:27-08', '2025-09-07 07:12:12-08', 1),
  (36, 'IRR-000036', 'Minister Spencer Chandra Herbert provided an update relevant to Burnaby-New Westminster, with ini...', 14, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Minister Spencer Chandra Herbert provided an update relevant to Burnaby-New Westminster, with initiatives connected to the IRR mandate and partners like First Nations Leadership Council, Council of the Haida Nation, UBCM. Regional stakeholders from Burnaby-New Westminster will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'It nudges long–term resilience, not just short–term fixes. People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days.', true, false, '2027-02-10', '2027-02-10', 2, '09:30:00', '12:30:00', 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Spencer Chandra Herbert summarized IRR actions in Burnaby-New Westminster, with partners like First Nations Leadership Council. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 14, 21, 4, 1, 1, '2024-12-03 02:28:51-08', '2026-02-24 11:26:34-08', 1),
  (37, 'INF-000037', 'Minister Bowinn Ma described delivery timelines for community and health capital projects in Suns...', 15, NULL, 'REGIONAL TOUR STOP: Minister Bowinn Ma described delivery timelines for community and health capital projects in Sunshine Coast, leveraging benefits agreements and BC Infrastructure Benefits to maximize local hiring. Projects will incorporate low-carbon construction materials and climate resilience standards. Regional stakeholders from Sunshine Coast will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'In practical terms: Community benefits agreements create apprenticeships close to home. Low–carbon building standards lock in lower operating costs for decades. It supports local hiring and keeps dollars circulating here.', true, true, '2027-10-04', '2027-10-04', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Embargoed until 09:00 PT on release day. Virtual technical briefing the day before.', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Regional tour stop: Minister Bowinn Ma summarized INF actions in Sunshine Coast, with partners like Transportation Investment Corporation. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 15, 22, 3, 1, 1, '2024-11-26 00:05:59-08', '2026-01-29 01:41:34-08', 1),
  (38, 'JEG-000038', 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Ravi Kahlon highlighted new trade diversification projects and a talent stra...', 17, NULL, 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Ravi Kahlon highlighted new trade diversification projects and a talent strategy for clean tech and life sciences in Sunshine Coast, delivered with Innovate BC and partners through Look West. The update included targeted supports for SMEs, export-readiness training, and investment attraction for anchor employers. Regional stakeholders from Sunshine Coast will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'If you live here: SME supports (exports, productivity, hiring) help firms keep people on during uncertainty. Less red tape and more coordination make it easier to plan ahead. Less paperwork, clearer timelines, fewer surprises.', false, true, '2027-05-01', '2027-05-01', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Rolling announcement series; this stop follows Prince George and precedes Kelowna.', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Open house: Minister Ravi Kahlon summarized JEDI actions in Sunshine Coast, with partners like Innovate BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 17, 24, 3, 1, 1, '2025-10-29 12:57:03-08', '2026-02-16 13:31:30-08', 1),
  (39, 'LAB-000039', 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Jennifer Whiteside announced worker-safety initiatives and updates to employ...', 18, NULL, 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Jennifer Whiteside announced worker-safety initiatives and updates to employment standards affecting Burnaby-New Westminster, in partnership with WorkSafeBC and labour stakeholders. The package includes protections for gig workers, anti-harassment measures and multilingual employer outreach. Regional stakeholders from Burnaby-New Westminster will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Stronger safety and fair–work rules protect gig and frontline workers without burying small employers.', false, false, '2027-02-26', '2027-02-26', 2, '14:00:00', '16:00:00', 2, 'Rolling announcement series; this stop follows Prince George and precedes Kelowna.', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Open house: Minister Jennifer Whiteside summarized LAB actions in Burnaby-New Westminster, with partners like WorkSafeBC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', true, NULL, NULL, 3, 3, NULL, NULL, 'global', 18, 25, 3, 1, 1, '2025-08-02 08:59:50-08', '2026-02-18 00:43:27-08', 1),
  (40, 'MIN-000040', 'Minister Jagrup Brar provided an update on critical-minerals roadmaps and permitting in Comox Val...', 19, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Minister Jagrup Brar provided an update on critical-minerals roadmaps and permitting in Comox Valley, aligning power access with BC Hydro and workforce partnerships for responsible development. The strategy advances downstream processing and Indigenous participation benefits agreements. Regional stakeholders from Comox Valley will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Why people care: Responsible permitting and power access let projects advance while protecting water and local values. Benefit agreements with Nations build durable partnerships. The changes are small on paper but add up across a year of errands, commitments and bills. It supports local hiring and keeps dollars circulating here.', false, false, '2027-04-10', '2027-04-10', 3, '14:30:00', '17:30:00', 3, 'Pushing back one week to sync with email campaign timeline; MO approved, date unconfirmed.', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Jagrup Brar summarized MIN actions in Comox Valley, with partners like Geoscience BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 19, 26, 3, 1, 1, '2025-05-06 21:45:31-08', '2026-02-15 22:46:50-08', 1),
  (41, 'PSFS-000041', 'Minister Jessie Sunner highlighted micro-credentials and co-op expansions in Whistler and Sea-to-...', 20, NULL, 'STAKEHOLDER CALL: Minister Jessie Sunner highlighted micro-credentials and co-op expansions in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky, supported by StudentAid BC and EducationPlannerBC, to align learners with high-demand jobs in tech, health and trades. New student housing and skills grants will reduce barriers for rural and Indigenous learners. Regional stakeholders from Whistler and Sea-to-Sky will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Community impact: Micro–credentials and co–ops align programs with real jobs; grads stay in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky. Less red tape and more coordination make it easier to plan ahead. It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns.', false, false, '2027-03-30', '2027-03-30', 1, '10:00:00', '13:00:00', 1, NULL, NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Stakeholder call: Minister Jessie Sunner summarized PSFS actions in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky, with partners like StudentAid BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 20, 27, 3, 1, 1, '2024-10-14 01:37:47-08', '2026-02-22 03:41:37-08', 1),
  (42, 'PSSG-000042', 'Minister Garry Begg announced expanded enforcement against organized crime and retail theft, coor...', 21, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Minister Garry Begg announced expanded enforcement against organized crime and retail theft, coordinated with BC RCMP and municipal police in East Kootenay (Cranbrook, Fernie) and supported by modernized information sharing. The program includes investments in community safety teams and better supports for victims and small businesses. Regional stakeholders from East Kootenay (Cranbrook, Fernie) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'More support for victims reduces re–traumatization and improves reporting. More support for victims reduces re–traumatization and improves reporting. It’s incremental, but tangible.', true, false, '2027-03-23', '2027-03-23', 2, '14:00:00', '16:00:00', 2, 'Tentative: first week of next month, subject to travel windows and weather.', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Garry Begg summarized PSSG actions in East Kootenay (Cranbrook, Fernie), with partners like BC RCMP. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 21, 28, 3, 1, 1, '2025-04-02 16:58:54-08', '2025-12-03 01:03:37-08', 1),
  (43, 'SDPR-000043', 'Minister Sheila Malcolmson announced improvements to disability assistance and employment service...', 22, NULL, 'REGIONAL TOUR STOP: Minister Sheila Malcolmson announced improvements to disability assistance and employment services in Maple Ridge-Pitt Meadows, coordinated through WorkBC and community partners to reduce barriers. The update included simplified applications, earnings exemptions and culturally responsive supports. Regional stakeholders from Maple Ridge-Pitt Meadows will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Why it matters: Simpler disability supports and WorkBC pathways reduce churn and paperwork fatigue. Simpler disability supports and WorkBC pathways reduce churn and paperwork fatigue. It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns.', false, false, NULL, NULL, 2, '14:45:00', '15:45:00', 2, 'Tentative: first week of next month, subject to travel windows and weather.', NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Regional tour stop: Minister Sheila Malcolmson summarized SDPR actions in Maple Ridge-Pitt Meadows, with partners like Service BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 22, 29, 3, 1, 1, '2025-11-14 02:38:04-08', '2026-02-18 16:05:54-08', 1),
  (44, 'TACS-000044', 'Minister Anne Kang announced destination development funding, film incentives and sport event sup...', 23, NULL, 'THIRD-PARTY EVENT: Minister Anne Kang announced destination development funding, film incentives and sport event support in Richmond, working with Destination BC and Creative BC to extend shoulder-season visits. Investments will improve accessibility, trail networks and cultural spaces in collaboration with local nations. Regional stakeholders from Richmond will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Destination upgrades and film incentives smooth out shoulder seasons–stable hours for hospitality workers in Richmond. Accessible trails and cultural spaces broaden who gets to enjoy B.C., residents first. It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns.', false, false, '2027-02-26', '2027-02-26', 3, '16:15:00', '17:00:00', 3, 'Pushing back one week to sync with email campaign timeline; MO approved, date unconfirmed.', NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Third-party event: Minister Anne Kang summarized TACS actions in Richmond, with partners like Destination BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 23, 30, 3, 1, 1, '2025-10-12 18:38:02-08', '2026-02-16 03:56:36-08', 1),
  (45, 'MOTT-000045', 'TECHNICAL BRIEFING: Minister Mike Farnworth outlined near-term upgrades to Highway 1 and transit ...', 24, NULL, 'TECHNICAL BRIEFING: Minister Mike Farnworth outlined near-term upgrades to Highway 1 and transit hubs, including new bus priority lanes in Kootenay Boundary, while continuing work with TransLink and BC Transit on ridership recovery and with BC Ferries on sailing reliability. The update included construction milestones for active transportation links and integrated fare pilots to simplify inter-regional travel. Regional stakeholders from Kootenay Boundary will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Safer corridors and active–transportation links open school and work options for people who don’t drive, cutting emissions with everyday trips. Kootenay Boundary commuters get faster, more reliable trips–bus lanes and integrated fares mean fewer missed connections and less time in traffic. The changes are small on paper but add up across a year of errands, commitments and bills. Less paperwork, clearer timelines, fewer surprises.', false, true, '2027-01-29', '2027-01-29', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Technical briefing: Minister Mike Farnworth summarized MOTI actions in Kootenay Boundary, with partners like TransLink. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 3, NULL, NULL, 'team', 24, 31, 3, 1, 1, '2025-09-01 08:13:42-08', '2026-02-10 18:36:33-08', 1),
  (46, 'WLRS-000046', 'Minister Randene Neill outlined watershed security actions in Boundary Country, integrating habit...', 25, NULL, 'MEDIA AVAIL: Minister Randene Neill outlined watershed security actions in Boundary Country, integrating habitat restoration with Living Lakes Canada and expanded data-sharing to support permitting and drought response. The plan strengthens cumulative effects management and inter-ministry coordination. Regional stakeholders from Boundary Country will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Short version: Watershed security and drought planning protect drinking water and farms in Boundary Country. Better data and permitting clarity speed up habitat fixes. Less red tape and more coordination make it easier to plan ahead. It’s incremental, but tangible.', false, false, '2027-02-27', '2027-02-27', 2, '10:00:00', '12:00:00', 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, 'Media avail: Minister Randene Neill summarized WLRS actions in Boundary Country, with partners like BC Parks. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', true, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 25, 32, 4, 1, 1, '2025-03-22 09:29:20-08', '2026-02-16 12:08:42-08', 1),
  (47, 'AF-000047', 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Lana Popham provided an update relevant to Comox Valley, with initiatives co...', 2, NULL, 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Lana Popham provided an update relevant to Comox Valley, with initiatives connected to the AF mandate and partners like BC Milk Marketing Board, Investment Agriculture Foundation, BC Farmers'' Markets. Regional stakeholders from Comox Valley will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting. Engagement will continue through webinars and in-person sessions to refine delivery details before rollout.', 'It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns. Less red tape and more coordination make it easier to plan ahead.', false, false, '2027-02-11', '2027-02-11', 3, '11:00:00', '13:00:00', 3, 'Pushing back one week to sync with email campaign timeline; MO approved, date unconfirmed.', NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Open house: Minister Lana Popham summarized AF actions in Comox Valley, with partners like BC Milk Marketing Board. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 2, 9, 3, 1, 1, '2025-04-05 02:34:13-08', '2025-05-27 00:29:39-08', 1),
  (48, 'AG-000048', 'OPEN HOUSE: Attorney General Niki Sharma introduced measures to streamline the Civil Resolution T...', 3, NULL, 'OPEN HOUSE: Attorney General Niki Sharma introduced measures to streamline the Civil Resolution Tribunal and bolster resources for the BC Prosecution Service, reducing delays while improving victim services coordination in Sooke and West Shore. Reforms include digital filing pilots and cross-agency protocols with public safety partners to tackle repeat violent offending. Regional stakeholders from Sooke and West Shore will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Digital filing and data–sharing cut backlogs so serious cases move quicker. Streamlined tribunals and prosecutions mean faster resolutions for victims and businesses–less time lost to paperwork.', false, false, '2027-03-15', '2027-03-15', 2, '14:30:00', '15:30:00', 2, 'Tentative: first week of next month, subject to travel windows and weather.', NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, 'Open house: Minister Niki Sharma summarized AG actions in Sooke and West Shore, with partners like BC Prosecution Service. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 3, 10, 1, 1, 1, '2024-11-24 07:23:18-08', '2026-02-18 11:56:04-08', 1),
  (49, 'MCFD-000049', 'Minister Jodie Wickens announced expanded supports for youth in care and children and youth with ...', 4, NULL, 'TWO-DAY GATHERING: Minister Jodie Wickens announced expanded supports for youth in care and children and youth with support needs in Prince George, co-designed with Indigenous partners and community agencies. The initiative strengthens culturally safe services and transitions to adulthood with housing and education pathways. Regional stakeholders from Prince George will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Bottom line– Co–design with Indigenous partners improves cultural safety and trust. Expanded CYWSN and youth–in–care supports close service gaps and ease transitions to housing, work and school. It’s incremental, but tangible.', false, false, '2027-08-16', '2027-08-16', 2, '13:00:00', '14:00:00', 2, 'Tentative: first week of next month, subject to travel windows and weather.', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Two-day gathering: Minister Jodie Wickens summarized CFD actions in Prince George, with partners like BCGEU. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 4, 11, 3, 1, 1, '2025-03-05 09:39:51-08', '2026-03-01 16:08:17-08', 1),
  (50, 'CITZ-000050', 'Minister Diana Gibson announced a digital service refresh for Service BC locations in Burnaby-New...', 5, NULL, 'REGIONAL TOUR STOP: Minister Diana Gibson announced a digital service refresh for Service BC locations in Burnaby-New Westminster, expanding identity verification, permitting portals and connectivity with the BCDevExchange community. The work advances secure-by-design standards and plain-language service improvements across channels. Regional stakeholders from Burnaby-New Westminster will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Service BC upgrades reduce lineups–more done online, fewer repeat visits. That means time back in people’s days and money kept in local pockets.', false, false, '2027-02-12', '2027-02-12', 2, '15:00:00', '17:00:00', 2, 'Rolling announcement series; this stop follows Prince George and precedes Kelowna.', NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Regional tour stop: Minister Diana Gibson summarized CITZ actions in Burnaby-New Westminster, with partners like BC Registries. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 5, 12, 4, 1, 1, '2025-03-15 03:56:08-08', '2026-02-18 17:19:59-08', 1),
  (51, 'ECC-000051', 'Minister Lisa Beare outlined new classroom additions and early learning spaces in Kootenay Bounda...', 6, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Minister Lisa Beare outlined new classroom additions and early learning spaces in Kootenay Boundary, coordinated with school districts and BCTF to support enrolment growth and workforce needs. Funding also supports seismic upgrades and inclusive education resources developed with local educators. Regional stakeholders from Kootenay Boundary will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'In practical terms: More classrooms and child care spaces in Kootenay Boundary reduce portables and waitlists. It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns.', true, false, '2027-02-27', '2027-02-27', 1, '14:45:00', '17:45:00', 1, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Lisa Beare summarized ECC actions in Kootenay Boundary, with partners like BC School Trustees Association. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 3, 3, NULL, NULL, 'global', 6, 13, 3, 1, 1, '2025-02-14 17:09:17-08', '2026-03-02 10:56:36-08', 1),
  (52, 'EMCR-000052', 'Minister Kelly Greene detailed seasonal preparedness for floods, drought and wildfire in Langley,...', 7, NULL, 'MEDIA AVAIL: Minister Kelly Greene detailed seasonal preparedness for floods, drought and wildfire in Langley, highlighting resources from PreparedBC and EmergencyInfoBC and community-level evacuation planning. Investments include modernized emergency operations centres and enhanced public alerting with local authorities. Regional stakeholders from Langley will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'For businesses: Better alerts, evacuation routes and EOC capacity in Langley save lives when floods or fires strike.', false, false, '2027-03-10', '2027-03-10', 2, '13:00:00', '15:00:00', 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Media avail: Minister Kelly Greene summarized EMCR actions in Langley, with partners like BC Wildfire Service. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 7, 14, 4, 1, 1, '2025-08-28 06:43:40-08', '2026-02-20 22:46:17-08', 1),
  (53, 'ECS-000053', 'Minister Adrian Dix outlined grid-scale investments with BC Hydro and industrial electrification ...', 8, NULL, 'BUDGET BACKGROUNDER: Minister Adrian Dix outlined grid-scale investments with BC Hydro and industrial electrification opportunities in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), advancing CleanBC goals and supporting new critical-minerals processing. The plan includes fast-tracked interconnections for future projects and expanded heat-pump incentives for homes and small businesses. Regional stakeholders from Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'What changes on the ground: Faster interconnections mean clean projects come online sooner, reducing energy costs over time. Grid upgrades and electrification cut industrial emissions and create skilled jobs in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat). More predictability; better service; safer communities.', true, false, '2026-12-31', '2026-12-31', 2, '15:30:00', '17:30:00', 2, 'Morning event preferred; avoid municipal budget deliberations week.', NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, 'Budget backgrounder: Minister Adrian Dix summarized ECS actions in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), with partners like BC Hydro. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'issues', true, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 8, 15, 3, 1, 1, '2024-11-26 01:05:40-08', '2026-02-03 08:57:58-08', 1),
  (54, 'EP-000054', 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Tamara Davidson announced expanded conservation investments and trail upgrad...', 9, NULL, 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Tamara Davidson announced expanded conservation investments and trail upgrades in Boundary Country, with BC Parks and the Conservation Officer Service enhancing access while supporting habitat and climate resilience. The ministry also highlighted permitting efficiencies through the Environmental Assessment Office for clean-economy projects. Regional stakeholders from Boundary Country will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'For families: Cleaner permitting for clean–economy projects pairs jobs with better environmental outcomes. Investing in climate resilience now avoids bigger repair bills after storms and fires. It supports local hiring and keeps dollars circulating here.', false, false, '2026-12-27', '2026-12-27', 2, '11:30:00', '14:30:00', 2, 'Embargoed until 09:00 PT on release day. Virtual technical briefing the day before.', NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Open house: Minister Tamara Davidson summarized EP actions in Boundary Country, with partners like BC Parks. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 3, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 9, 16, 3, 1, 1, '2025-12-11 20:16:10-08', '2026-02-16 00:21:49-08', 1),
  (55, 'FIN-000055', 'Minister Brenda Bailey previewed fiscal guardrails and targeted affordability measures, noting on...', 10, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Minister Brenda Bailey previewed fiscal guardrails and targeted affordability measures, noting ongoing coordination with BC Assessment and InBC to support productivity and jobs across Nanaimo amid tariff volatility. Measures include focused relief for low- and fixed-income households and disciplined capital planning to protect core services. Regional stakeholders from Nanaimo will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Bottom line– Fiscal guardrails matter: they reduce risk of sudden cuts to hospitals, schools and transit when volatility hits. Targeted relief cushions households from rising costs while keeping capital projects moving–protecting services people rely on. It supports local hiring and keeps dollars circulating here.', false, true, '2027-02-21', '2027-02-21', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Tentative: first week of next month, subject to travel windows and weather.', NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Brenda Bailey summarized FIN actions in Nanaimo, with partners like BC Lottery Corporation. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 10, 17, 3, 1, 1, '2025-12-02 02:56:44-08', '2026-01-29 13:35:00-08', 1),
  (56, 'FOR-000056', 'TECHNICAL BRIEFING: Minister Ravi Parmar discussed wildfire readiness and fibre supply certainty ...', 11, NULL, 'TECHNICAL BRIEFING: Minister Ravi Parmar discussed wildfire readiness and fibre supply certainty in Cowichan Valley, including community resilience projects and partnerships with First Nations and BC Timber Sales. The briefing addressed support for affected workers, value-added manufacturing, and steps to accelerate reforestation. Regional stakeholders from Cowichan Valley will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'What changes on the ground: Support for value–added manufacturing diversifies jobs beyond log exports. It’s incremental, but tangible.', false, false, '2027-04-11', '2027-04-11', 2, '11:45:00', '14:45:00', 2, 'Targeting late Q1; coordinating venues with local partners. Media advisory to follow.', NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Technical briefing: Minister Ravi Parmar summarized FOR actions in Cowichan Valley, with partners like BC Timber Sales. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 11, 18, 3, 1, 1, '2025-11-15 13:08:02-08', '2026-01-30 11:37:35-08', 1),
  (57, 'HLTH-000057', 'Minister Josie Osborne provided an update on primary care access and ER stabilization in Columbia...', 12, NULL, 'STAKEHOLDER CALL: Minister Josie Osborne provided an update on primary care access and ER stabilization in Columbia-Shuswap, highlighting new Urgent and Primary Care Centre hours and Island-wide recruitment initiatives with health authorities like Island Health. The announcement also referenced ongoing work to integrate mental-health and addictions services within the broader care system. Regional stakeholders from Columbia-Shuswap will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Short version: Recruitment wins translate to fewer closures and shorter distances to care for rural patients. The changes are small on paper but add up across a year of errands, commitments and bills. It nudges long–term resilience, not just short–term fixes.', false, true, '2027-02-02', '2027-02-02', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Morning event preferred; avoid municipal budget deliberations week.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Stakeholder call: Minister Josie Osborne summarized HLTH actions in Columbia-Shuswap, with partners like PHSA. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 3, NULL, NULL, 'team', 12, 19, 3, 1, 1, '2025-04-07 21:15:42-08', '2025-07-24 01:57:22-08', 1),
  (58, 'HMA-000058', 'Minister Christine Boyle confirmed additional BC Builds sites and transit-oriented development pa...', 13, NULL, 'COMMUNITY ROUNDTABLE: Minister Christine Boyle confirmed additional BC Builds sites and transit-oriented development partnerships in Kootenay Boundary, advancing gentle density reforms under the MUNI file with local governments. Work with BC Housing and the BC Rent Bank network will target rental supply, student housing, and non-market homes aligned to community plans. Regional stakeholders from Kootenay Boundary will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Bottom line– Fast–tracked rentals and gentle density near transit in Kootenay Boundary chip away at waitlists and let workers live closer to jobs. Clear rules reduce rezoning fights and speed up permits so homes show up years, not decades, sooner. It supports local hiring and keeps dollars circulating here.', false, false, '2027-05-24', '2027-05-24', 1, '13:30:00', '14:30:00', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Community roundtable: Minister Christine Boyle summarized HMA actions in Kootenay Boundary, with partners like BC Housing. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 3, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 13, 20, 3, 1, 1, '2024-12-02 13:39:47-08', '2026-02-28 22:07:08-08', 1),
  (59, 'IRR-000059', 'Minister Spencer Chandra Herbert provided an update relevant to Chilliwack-Hope, with initiatives...', 14, NULL, 'TWO-DAY GATHERING: Minister Spencer Chandra Herbert provided an update relevant to Chilliwack-Hope, with initiatives connected to the IRR mandate and partners like First Nations Leadership Council, Council of the Haida Nation, UBCM. Regional stakeholders from Chilliwack-Hope will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Community impact: That means time back in people’s days and money kept in local pockets. Less red tape and more coordination make it easier to plan ahead. That means time back in people’s days and money kept in local pockets.', false, true, '2027-04-03', '2027-04-03', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Morning event preferred; avoid municipal budget deliberations week.', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Two-day gathering: Minister Spencer Chandra Herbert summarized IRR actions in Chilliwack-Hope, with partners like First Nations Leadership Council. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 14, 21, 4, 1, 1, '2024-12-15 05:51:51-08', '2026-03-03 00:26:24-08', 1),
  (60, 'INF-000060', 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Bowinn Ma described delivery timelines for community and health capital proj...', 15, NULL, 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Bowinn Ma described delivery timelines for community and health capital projects in Esquimalt, leveraging benefits agreements and BC Infrastructure Benefits to maximize local hiring. Projects will incorporate low-carbon construction materials and climate resilience standards. Regional stakeholders from Esquimalt will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Community benefits agreements create apprenticeships close to home. On–time capital builds mean local jobs now and modern hospitals, schools and community hubs later in Esquimalt.', false, false, '2027-12-19', '2027-12-19', 1, '16:15:00', '17:00:00', 1, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, 'Open house: Minister Bowinn Ma summarized INF actions in Esquimalt, with partners like Transportation Investment Corporation. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 15, 22, 3, 1, 1, '2025-11-23 23:59:21-08', '2026-02-23 18:31:51-08', 1),
  (61, 'JEG-000061', 'Minister Ravi Kahlon highlighted new trade diversification projects and a talent strategy for cle...', 17, NULL, 'THIRD-PARTY EVENT: Minister Ravi Kahlon highlighted new trade diversification projects and a talent strategy for clean tech and life sciences in Prince George, delivered with Innovate BC and partners through Look West. The update included targeted supports for SMEs, export-readiness training, and investment attraction for anchor employers. Regional stakeholders from Prince George will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'In practical terms: SME supports (exports, productivity, hiring) help firms keep people on during uncertainty. Talent pipelines in clean tech and life sciences connect grads to careers at home. It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns.', false, false, '2027-03-11', '2027-03-11', 3, '13:30:00', '16:30:00', 3, 'Pushing back one week to sync with email campaign timeline; MO approved, date unconfirmed.', NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, 'Third-party event: Minister Ravi Kahlon summarized JEDI actions in Prince George, with partners like Innovate BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 3, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 17, 24, 3, 1, 1, '2024-12-22 07:17:10-08', '2026-02-11 21:55:47-08', 1),
  (62, 'LAB-000062', 'Minister Jennifer Whiteside announced worker-safety initiatives and updates to employment standar...', 18, NULL, 'COMMUNITY ROUNDTABLE: Minister Jennifer Whiteside announced worker-safety initiatives and updates to employment standards affecting Richmond, in partnership with WorkSafeBC and labour stakeholders. The package includes protections for gig workers, anti-harassment measures and multilingual employer outreach. Regional stakeholders from Richmond will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'In practical terms: Stronger safety and fair–work rules protect gig and frontline workers without burying small employers. Anti–harassment measures and multilingual outreach make rights real on the shop floor. People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days.', false, true, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, 'Community roundtable: Minister Jennifer Whiteside summarized LAB actions in Richmond, with partners like WorkSafeBC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 18, 25, 3, 1, 1, '2025-10-27 06:52:58-08', '2026-02-18 01:54:30-08', 1),
  (63, 'MIN-000063', 'Minister Jagrup Brar provided an update on critical-minerals roadmaps and permitting in Boundary ...', 19, NULL, 'BUDGET BACKGROUNDER: Minister Jagrup Brar provided an update on critical-minerals roadmaps and permitting in Boundary Country, aligning power access with BC Hydro and workforce partnerships for responsible development. The strategy advances downstream processing and Indigenous participation benefits agreements. Regional stakeholders from Boundary Country will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'For locals: Responsible permitting and power access let projects advance while protecting water and local values. It supports local hiring and keeps dollars circulating here.', false, true, '2027-02-05', '2027-02-05', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Targeting late Q1; coordinating venues with local partners. Media advisory to follow.', NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, 'Budget backgrounder: Minister Jagrup Brar summarized MIN actions in Boundary Country, with partners like Geoscience BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 3, NULL, NULL, 'global', 19, 26, 3, 1, 1, '2025-03-14 06:25:21-08', '2026-02-15 07:14:01-08', 1),
  (64, 'PSFS-000064', 'Minister Jessie Sunner highlighted micro-credentials and co-op expansions in Prince George, suppo...', 20, NULL, 'PHOTO-OP & MINISTRY NR: Minister Jessie Sunner highlighted micro-credentials and co-op expansions in Prince George, supported by StudentAid BC and EducationPlannerBC, to align learners with high-demand jobs in tech, health and trades. New student housing and skills grants will reduce barriers for rural and Indigenous learners. Regional stakeholders from Prince George will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Lower barriers for rural and Indigenous learners mean more local talent pipelines. More predictability; better service; safer communities.', false, false, '2027-06-03', '2027-06-03', 2, '12:15:00', '14:15:00', 2, 'Rolling announcement series; this stop follows Prince George and precedes Kelowna.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Photo-op & ministry nr: Minister Jessie Sunner summarized PSFS actions in Prince George, with partners like StudentAid BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 20, 27, 3, 1, 1, '2025-01-18 08:22:41-08', '2026-02-18 23:19:31-08', 1),
  (65, 'PSSG-000065', 'Minister Garry Begg announced expanded enforcement against organized crime and retail theft, coor...', 21, NULL, 'TWO-DAY GATHERING: Minister Garry Begg announced expanded enforcement against organized crime and retail theft, coordinated with BC RCMP and municipal police in Metro Vancouver and supported by modernized information sharing. The program includes investments in community safety teams and better supports for victims and small businesses. Regional stakeholders from Metro Vancouver will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'For locals: Modern info–sharing helps police focus on repeat violent offenders instead of administrative churn. Less red tape and more coordination make it easier to plan ahead.', false, false, '2027-07-13', '2027-07-13', 2, '14:15:00', '16:15:00', 2, 'Embargoed until 09:00 PT on release day. Virtual technical briefing the day before.', NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, 'Two-day gathering: Minister Garry Begg summarized PSSG actions in Metro Vancouver, with partners like BC RCMP. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 21, 28, 4, 1, 1, '2025-11-01 08:11:37-08', '2025-12-31 17:21:01-08', 1),
  (66, 'SDPR-000066', 'Minister Sheila Malcolmson announced improvements to disability assistance and employment service...', 22, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Minister Sheila Malcolmson announced improvements to disability assistance and employment services in Maple Ridge-Pitt Meadows, coordinated through WorkBC and community partners to reduce barriers. The update included simplified applications, earnings exemptions and culturally responsive supports. Regional stakeholders from Maple Ridge-Pitt Meadows will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Here’s the significance: Simpler disability supports and WorkBC pathways reduce churn and paperwork fatigue. Less red tape and more coordination make it easier to plan ahead.', false, true, '2027-12-19', '2027-12-19', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Week of next full moon–exact date pending room availability in community hall.', NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Sheila Malcolmson summarized SDPR actions in Maple Ridge-Pitt Meadows, with partners like Service BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 22, 29, 3, 1, 1, '2025-08-23 23:50:20-08', '2026-02-16 03:38:27-08', 1),
  (67, 'TACS-000067', 'Minister Anne Kang announced destination development funding, film incentives and sport event sup...', 23, NULL, 'THIRD-PARTY EVENT: Minister Anne Kang announced destination development funding, film incentives and sport event support in Victoria, working with Destination BC and Creative BC to extend shoulder-season visits. Investments will improve accessibility, trail networks and cultural spaces in collaboration with local nations. Regional stakeholders from Victoria will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'In practical terms: Events bring visitors, but also community pride and volunteer energy. Accessible trails and cultural spaces broaden who gets to enjoy B.C., residents first. That means time back in people’s days and money kept in local pockets.', false, true, '2027-05-29', '2027-05-29', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Third-party event: Minister Anne Kang summarized TACS actions in Victoria, with partners like Destination BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 23, 30, 3, 1, 1, '2024-09-20 06:16:02-08', '2025-02-15 03:24:57-08', 1),
  (68, 'MOTT-000068', 'Minister Mike Farnworth outlined near-term upgrades to Highway 1 and transit hubs, including new ...', 24, NULL, 'STAKEHOLDER CALL: Minister Mike Farnworth outlined near-term upgrades to Highway 1 and transit hubs, including new bus priority lanes in Saanich Peninsula, while continuing work with TransLink and BC Transit on ridership recovery and with BC Ferries on sailing reliability. The update included construction milestones for active transportation links and integrated fare pilots to simplify inter-regional travel. Regional stakeholders from Saanich Peninsula will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'For families: Better ferry/transit alignment eases weekend bottlenecks and helps shift workers make early runs without costly detours. Saanich Peninsula commuters get faster, more reliable trips–bus lanes and integrated fares mean fewer missed connections and less time in traffic. The changes are small on paper but add up across a year of errands, commitments and bills. That means time back in people’s days and money kept in local pockets.', false, false, '2027-04-19', '2027-04-19', 2, '16:45:00', '17:00:00', 2, 'Rolling announcement series; this stop follows Prince George and precedes Kelowna.', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Stakeholder call: Minister Mike Farnworth summarized MOTI actions in Saanich Peninsula, with partners like TransLink. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 24, 31, 6, 1, 1, '2024-10-24 23:47:42-08', '2026-02-18 17:43:46-08', 1),
  (69, 'WLRS-000069', 'Minister Randene Neill outlined watershed security actions in Esquimalt, integrating habitat rest...', 25, NULL, 'TWO-DAY GATHERING: Minister Randene Neill outlined watershed security actions in Esquimalt, integrating habitat restoration with Living Lakes Canada and expanded data-sharing to support permitting and drought response. The plan strengthens cumulative effects management and inter-ministry coordination. Regional stakeholders from Esquimalt will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Cumulative–effects work reduces conflict and surprises later. People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days.', false, false, NULL, NULL, 1, '09:30:00', '12:30:00', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Two-day gathering: Minister Randene Neill summarized WLRS actions in Esquimalt, with partners like BC Parks. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', true, NULL, NULL, 2, 3, NULL, NULL, 'team', 25, 32, 3, 1, 1, '2024-10-26 21:58:21-08', '2026-02-24 00:54:57-08', 1),
  (70, 'AF-000070', 'Minister Lana Popham provided an update relevant to Boundary Country, with initiatives connected ...', 2, NULL, 'COMMUNITY ROUNDTABLE: Minister Lana Popham provided an update relevant to Boundary Country, with initiatives connected to the AF mandate and partners like BC Milk Marketing Board, Investment Agriculture Foundation, BC Farmers'' Markets. Regional stakeholders from Boundary Country will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Here’s the significance: The changes are small on paper but add up across a year of errands, commitments and bills. It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns.', false, false, '2027-05-14', '2027-05-14', 3, '10:45:00', '12:45:00', 3, 'Pushing back one week to sync with email campaign timeline; MO approved, date unconfirmed.', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Community roundtable: Minister Lana Popham summarized AF actions in Boundary Country, with partners like BC Milk Marketing Board. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 2, 9, 6, 1, 1, '2025-08-04 16:19:42-08', '2026-01-05 03:46:57-08', 1),
  (71, 'AG-000071', 'TECHNICAL BRIEFING: Attorney General Niki Sharma introduced measures to streamline the Civil Reso...', 3, NULL, 'TECHNICAL BRIEFING: Attorney General Niki Sharma introduced measures to streamline the Civil Resolution Tribunal and bolster resources for the BC Prosecution Service, reducing delays while improving victim services coordination in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat). Reforms include digital filing pilots and cross-agency protocols with public safety partners to tackle repeat violent offending. Regional stakeholders from Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'For businesses: Clearer pathways help people self–resolve disputes without costly court time. Streamlined tribunals and prosecutions mean faster resolutions for victims and businesses–less time lost to paperwork. People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days. More predictability; better service; safer communities.', false, false, '2027-12-11', '2027-12-11', 1, '15:00:00', '17:00:00', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Technical briefing: Minister Niki Sharma summarized AG actions in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), with partners like BC Prosecution Service. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 3, 10, 3, 1, 1, '2025-11-04 13:42:24-08', '2026-02-11 09:35:08-08', 1),
  (72, 'MCFD-000072', 'Minister Jodie Wickens announced expanded supports for youth in care and children and youth with ...', 4, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Minister Jodie Wickens announced expanded supports for youth in care and children and youth with support needs in Cowichan Valley, co-designed with Indigenous partners and community agencies. The initiative strengthens culturally safe services and transitions to adulthood with housing and education pathways. Regional stakeholders from Cowichan Valley will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Why it matters: Stability for caregivers and better navigation reduce crisis cycling. Expanded CYWSN and youth–in–care supports close service gaps and ease transitions to housing, work and school. Less red tape and more coordination make it easier to plan ahead.', true, false, '2027-02-20', '2027-02-20', 1, '13:15:00', '16:15:00', 1, NULL, NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Jodie Wickens summarized CFD actions in Cowichan Valley, with partners like BCGEU. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 3, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 4, 11, 3, 1, 1, '2024-12-22 17:53:00-08', '2025-07-18 19:36:19-08', 1),
  (73, 'CITZ-000073', 'Minister Diana Gibson announced a digital service refresh for Service BC locations in Langley, ex...', 5, NULL, 'REGIONAL TOUR STOP: Minister Diana Gibson announced a digital service refresh for Service BC locations in Langley, expanding identity verification, permitting portals and connectivity with the BCDevExchange community. The work advances secure-by-design standards and plain-language service improvements across channels. Regional stakeholders from Langley will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'For families: Plain–language, secure–by–design services make government simpler and safer to use. It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns.', false, false, '2027-08-11', '2027-08-11', 2, '10:15:00', '13:15:00', 2, 'Tentative: first week of next month, subject to travel windows and weather.', NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, 'Regional tour stop: Minister Diana Gibson summarized CITZ actions in Langley, with partners like BC Registries. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 3, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 5, 12, 3, 1, 1, '2025-09-05 14:28:28-08', '2026-02-17 18:38:41-08', 1),
  (74, 'ECC-000074', 'Minister Lisa Beare outlined new classroom additions and early learning spaces in Sunshine Coast,...', 6, NULL, 'BUDGET BACKGROUNDER: Minister Lisa Beare outlined new classroom additions and early learning spaces in Sunshine Coast, coordinated with school districts and BCTF to support enrolment growth and workforce needs. Funding also supports seismic upgrades and inclusive education resources developed with local educators. Regional stakeholders from Sunshine Coast will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'For families: More classrooms and child care spaces in Sunshine Coast reduce portables and waitlists. Less red tape and more coordination make it easier to plan ahead.', false, false, '2027-05-13', '2027-05-13', 2, '12:45:00', '14:45:00', 2, 'Week of next full moon–exact date pending room availability in community hall.', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Budget backgrounder: Minister Lisa Beare summarized ECC actions in Sunshine Coast, with partners like BC School Trustees Association. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 6, 13, 3, 1, 1, '2025-12-21 09:32:42-08', '2026-02-03 23:10:42-08', 1),
  (75, 'EMCR-000075', 'Minister Kelly Greene detailed seasonal preparedness for floods, drought and wildfire in Peace (F...', 7, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Minister Kelly Greene detailed seasonal preparedness for floods, drought and wildfire in Peace (Fort St. John, Dawson Creek), highlighting resources from PreparedBC and EmergencyInfoBC and community-level evacuation planning. Investments include modernized emergency operations centres and enhanced public alerting with local authorities. Regional stakeholders from Peace (Fort St. John, Dawson Creek) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Co–ordinated planning reduces overlap and confusion between agencies on bad days. Less red tape and more coordination make it easier to plan ahead.', false, false, '2027-03-01', '2027-03-01', 2, '15:00:00', '17:00:00', 2, 'Tentative: first week of next month, subject to travel windows and weather.', NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Kelly Greene summarized EMCR actions in Peace (Fort St. John, Dawson Creek), with partners like BC Wildfire Service. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 3, NULL, NULL, 'team', 7, 14, 3, 1, 1, '2025-10-21 06:09:01-08', '2026-02-14 07:43:19-08', 1),
  (76, 'ECS-000076', 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Adrian Dix outlined grid-scale investments with BC Hydro and industrial elec...', 8, NULL, 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Adrian Dix outlined grid-scale investments with BC Hydro and industrial electrification opportunities in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), advancing CleanBC goals and supporting new critical-minerals processing. The plan includes fast-tracked interconnections for future projects and expanded heat-pump incentives for homes and small businesses. Regional stakeholders from Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Why people care: Heat–pump incentives lower household bills and improve comfort during heat waves and cold snaps.', true, true, '2027-04-08', '2027-04-08', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Embargoed until 09:00 PT on release day. Virtual technical briefing the day before.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Open house: Minister Adrian Dix summarized ECS actions in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), with partners like BC Hydro. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 3, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 8, 15, 3, 1, 1, '2025-04-24 02:29:26-08', '2026-03-03 18:36:09-08', 1),
  (77, 'EP-000077', 'Minister Tamara Davidson announced expanded conservation investments and trail upgrades in Okanag...', 9, NULL, 'BUDGET BACKGROUNDER: Minister Tamara Davidson announced expanded conservation investments and trail upgrades in Okanagan (Kelowna, Vernon, Penticton), with BC Parks and the Conservation Officer Service enhancing access while supporting habitat and climate resilience. The ministry also highlighted permitting efficiencies through the Environmental Assessment Office for clean-economy projects. Regional stakeholders from Okanagan (Kelowna, Vernon, Penticton) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Upgraded trails and habitat work in Okanagan (Kelowna, Vernon, Penticton) balance access and conservation–good for residents, tourism and wildlife. People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days. That means time back in people’s days and money kept in local pockets.', false, false, '2027-03-11', '2027-03-11', 2, '15:15:00', '16:15:00', 2, 'Rolling announcement series; this stop follows Prince George and precedes Kelowna.', NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Budget backgrounder: Minister Tamara Davidson summarized EP actions in Okanagan (Kelowna, Vernon, Penticton), with partners like BC Parks. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 9, 16, 3, 1, 1, '2025-05-16 12:15:09-08', '2026-01-25 22:44:24-08', 1),
  (78, 'FIN-000078', 'Minister Brenda Bailey previewed fiscal guardrails and targeted affordability measures, noting on...', 10, NULL, 'THIRD-PARTY EVENT: Minister Brenda Bailey previewed fiscal guardrails and targeted affordability measures, noting ongoing coordination with BC Assessment and InBC to support productivity and jobs across Nanaimo amid tariff volatility. Measures include focused relief for low- and fixed-income households and disciplined capital planning to protect core services. Regional stakeholders from Nanaimo will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Fiscal guardrails matter: they reduce risk of sudden cuts to hospitals, schools and transit when volatility hits. Targeted relief cushions households from rising costs while keeping capital projects moving–protecting services people rely on. It nudges long–term resilience, not just short–term fixes.', true, false, '2027-05-04', '2027-05-04', 2, '13:00:00', '16:00:00', 2, 'Week of next full moon–exact date pending room availability in community hall.', NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, 'Third-party event: Minister Brenda Bailey summarized FIN actions in Nanaimo, with partners like BC Lottery Corporation. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 10, 17, 1, 1, 1, '2025-10-28 05:51:44-08', '2026-02-18 03:49:27-08', 1),
  (79, 'FOR-000079', 'Minister Ravi Parmar discussed wildfire readiness and fibre supply certainty in Saanich Peninsula...', 11, NULL, 'PHOTO-OP & MINISTRY NR: Minister Ravi Parmar discussed wildfire readiness and fibre supply certainty in Saanich Peninsula, including community resilience projects and partnerships with First Nations and BC Timber Sales. The briefing addressed support for affected workers, value-added manufacturing, and steps to accelerate reforestation. Regional stakeholders from Saanich Peninsula will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Community impact: Wildfire readiness and fibre–supply clarity help mills plan shifts and keep crews working in Saanich Peninsula. Support for value–added manufacturing diversifies jobs beyond log exports. It nudges long–term resilience, not just short–term fixes.', false, false, '2027-12-17', '2027-12-17', 2, '16:45:00', '17:00:00', 2, 'Targeting late Q1; coordinating venues with local partners. Media advisory to follow.', NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Photo-op & ministry nr: Minister Ravi Parmar summarized FOR actions in Saanich Peninsula, with partners like BC Timber Sales. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 3, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 11, 18, 3, 1, 1, '2025-12-17 14:08:51-08', '2026-02-18 07:58:54-08', 1),
  (80, 'HLTH-000080', 'Minister Josie Osborne provided an update on primary care access and ER stabilization in Cariboo ...', 12, NULL, 'BUDGET BACKGROUNDER: Minister Josie Osborne provided an update on primary care access and ER stabilization in Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel), highlighting new Urgent and Primary Care Centre hours and Island-wide recruitment initiatives with health authorities like Island Health. The announcement also referenced ongoing work to integrate mental-health and addictions services within the broader care system. Regional stakeholders from Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'In a nutshell: More predictable clinic hours and integrated mental–health supports mean people get help sooner, not just at crisis points. Stabilizing ERs and primary care in Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel) reduces long waits and expensive out–of–town travel, especially for seniors and families with kids. It nudges long–term resilience, not just short–term fixes.', false, false, '2026-12-06', '2026-12-06', 2, '12:15:00', '15:15:00', 2, 'Week of next full moon–exact date pending room availability in community hall.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Budget backgrounder: Minister Josie Osborne summarized HLTH actions in Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel), with partners like PHSA. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 12, 19, 3, 1, 1, '2024-10-01 14:39:52-08', '2026-01-31 17:38:20-08', 1),
  (81, 'HMA-000081', 'Minister Christine Boyle confirmed additional BC Builds sites and transit-oriented development pa...', 13, NULL, 'THIRD-PARTY EVENT: Minister Christine Boyle confirmed additional BC Builds sites and transit-oriented development partnerships in Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel), advancing gentle density reforms under the MUNI file with local governments. Work with BC Housing and the BC Rent Bank network will target rental supply, student housing, and non-market homes aligned to community plans. Regional stakeholders from Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'BC Builds sites bring predictable delivery and more non–market options–stability for families, students, and seniors on fixed incomes. Fast–tracked rentals and gentle density near transit in Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel) chip away at waitlists and let workers live closer to jobs. It supports local hiring and keeps dollars circulating here.', true, false, '2027-08-13', '2027-08-13', 2, '12:45:00', '14:45:00', 2, 'Targeting late Q1; coordinating venues with local partners. Media advisory to follow.', NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, 'Third-party event: Minister Christine Boyle summarized HMA actions in Cariboo (Williams Lake, Quesnel), with partners like BC Housing. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 3, NULL, NULL, 'team', 13, 20, 3, 1, 1, '2025-11-13 23:55:30-08', '2026-02-03 17:28:57-08', 1),
  (82, 'IRR-000082', 'Minister Spencer Chandra Herbert provided an update relevant to Saanich Peninsula, with initiativ...', 14, NULL, 'STAKEHOLDER CALL: Minister Spencer Chandra Herbert provided an update relevant to Saanich Peninsula, with initiatives connected to the IRR mandate and partners like First Nations Leadership Council, Council of the Haida Nation, UBCM. Regional stakeholders from Saanich Peninsula will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'For businesses: It’s incremental, but tangible. The changes are small on paper but add up across a year of errands, commitments and bills. It nudges long–term resilience, not just short–term fixes.', false, true, '2027-09-05', '2027-09-05', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Targeting late Q1; coordinating venues with local partners. Media advisory to follow.', NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Stakeholder call: Minister Spencer Chandra Herbert summarized IRR actions in Saanich Peninsula, with partners like First Nations Leadership Council. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 14, 21, 1, 1, 1, '2024-10-28 16:31:40-08', '2025-12-01 20:17:49-08', 1),
  (83, 'INF-000083', 'Minister Bowinn Ma described delivery timelines for community and health capital projects in Whis...', 15, NULL, 'TWO-DAY GATHERING: Minister Bowinn Ma described delivery timelines for community and health capital projects in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky, leveraging benefits agreements and BC Infrastructure Benefits to maximize local hiring. Projects will incorporate low-carbon construction materials and climate resilience standards. Regional stakeholders from Whistler and Sea-to-Sky will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'On–time capital builds mean local jobs now and modern hospitals, schools and community hubs later in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky. People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days. It nudges long–term resilience, not just short–term fixes.', false, true, '2027-04-04', '2027-04-04', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Targeting late Q1; coordinating venues with local partners. Media advisory to follow.', NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Two-day gathering: Minister Bowinn Ma summarized INF actions in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky, with partners like Transportation Investment Corporation. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', true, NULL, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 15, 22, 3, 1, 1, '2025-02-23 09:15:17-08', '2026-02-24 03:47:49-08', 1),
  (84, 'JEG-000084', 'Minister Ravi Kahlon highlighted new trade diversification projects and a talent strategy for cle...', 17, NULL, 'PHOTO-OP & MINISTRY NR: Minister Ravi Kahlon highlighted new trade diversification projects and a talent strategy for clean tech and life sciences in Langley, delivered with Innovate BC and partners through Look West. The update included targeted supports for SMEs, export-readiness training, and investment attraction for anchor employers. Regional stakeholders from Langley will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'For locals: SME supports (exports, productivity, hiring) help firms keep people on during uncertainty. It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns.', false, false, '2027-06-13', '2027-06-13', 2, '16:15:00', '17:15:00', 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, 'Photo-op & ministry nr: Minister Ravi Kahlon summarized JEDI actions in Langley, with partners like Innovate BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 17, 24, 6, 1, 1, '2025-04-04 12:44:09-08', '2025-08-01 02:08:09-08', 1),
  (85, 'LAB-000085', 'Minister Jennifer Whiteside announced worker-safety initiatives and updates to employment standar...', 18, NULL, 'THIRD-PARTY EVENT: Minister Jennifer Whiteside announced worker-safety initiatives and updates to employment standards affecting Kootenay Boundary, in partnership with WorkSafeBC and labour stakeholders. The package includes protections for gig workers, anti-harassment measures and multilingual employer outreach. Regional stakeholders from Kootenay Boundary will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Bottom line– Clearer standards reduce disputes and level the playing field. People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days.', false, true, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Morning event preferred; avoid municipal budget deliberations week.', NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Third-party event: Minister Jennifer Whiteside summarized LAB actions in Kootenay Boundary, with partners like WorkSafeBC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 18, 25, 6, 1, 1, '2025-06-24 13:03:13-08', '2026-02-18 13:21:34-08', 1),
  (86, 'MIN-000086', 'TECHNICAL BRIEFING: Minister Jagrup Brar provided an update on critical-minerals roadmaps and per...', 19, NULL, 'TECHNICAL BRIEFING: Minister Jagrup Brar provided an update on critical-minerals roadmaps and permitting in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), aligning power access with BC Hydro and workforce partnerships for responsible development. The strategy advances downstream processing and Indigenous participation benefits agreements. Regional stakeholders from Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'If you live here: Benefit agreements with Nations build durable partnerships. Downstream processing keeps more value and jobs in B.C., not shipped overseas. It’s incremental, but tangible.', false, false, '2027-03-04', '2027-03-04', 2, '12:15:00', '15:15:00', 2, 'Week of next full moon–exact date pending room availability in community hall.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Technical briefing: Minister Jagrup Brar summarized MIN actions in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), with partners like Geoscience BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 19, 26, 3, 1, 1, '2024-11-30 18:24:30-08', '2026-02-12 18:44:01-08', 1),
  (87, 'PSFS-000087', 'Minister Jessie Sunner highlighted micro-credentials and co-op expansions in East Kootenay (Cranb...', 20, NULL, 'COMMUNITY ROUNDTABLE: Minister Jessie Sunner highlighted micro-credentials and co-op expansions in East Kootenay (Cranbrook, Fernie), supported by StudentAid BC and EducationPlannerBC, to align learners with high-demand jobs in tech, health and trades. New student housing and skills grants will reduce barriers for rural and Indigenous learners. Regional stakeholders from East Kootenay (Cranbrook, Fernie) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Bottom line– Lower barriers for rural and Indigenous learners mean more local talent pipelines. New student beds free up rental stock and shorten commutes. It supports local hiring and keeps dollars circulating here.', false, true, '2027-04-12', '2027-04-12', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Rolling announcement series; this stop follows Prince George and precedes Kelowna.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Community roundtable: Minister Jessie Sunner summarized PSFS actions in East Kootenay (Cranbrook, Fernie), with partners like StudentAid BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 3, NULL, NULL, 'global', 20, 27, 1, 1, 1, '2025-02-01 12:54:57-08', '2026-02-22 22:11:27-08', 1),
  (88, 'PSSG-000088', 'TECHNICAL BRIEFING: Minister Garry Begg announced expanded enforcement against organized crime an...', 21, NULL, 'TECHNICAL BRIEFING: Minister Garry Begg announced expanded enforcement against organized crime and retail theft, coordinated with BC RCMP and municipal police in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky and supported by modernized information sharing. The program includes investments in community safety teams and better supports for victims and small businesses. Regional stakeholders from Whistler and Sea-to-Sky will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Smarter enforcement against organized theft helps small retailers and restores confidence in downtowns. Modern info–sharing helps police focus on repeat violent offenders instead of administrative churn. The changes are small on paper but add up across a year of errands, commitments and bills. It’s incremental, but tangible.', false, true, '2027-08-08', '2027-08-08', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Tentative: first week of next month, subject to travel windows and weather.', NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Technical briefing: Minister Garry Begg summarized PSSG actions in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky, with partners like BC RCMP. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 3, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 21, 28, 3, 1, 1, '2024-12-27 19:57:14-08', '2026-02-10 23:47:34-08', 1),
  (89, 'SDPR-000089', 'Minister Sheila Malcolmson announced improvements to disability assistance and employment service...', 22, NULL, 'TWO-DAY GATHERING: Minister Sheila Malcolmson announced improvements to disability assistance and employment services in Sunshine Coast, coordinated through WorkBC and community partners to reduce barriers. The update included simplified applications, earnings exemptions and culturally responsive supports. Regional stakeholders from Sunshine Coast will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'If you live here: Earnings exemptions help people keep more of what they earn while they stabilize. People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days. It helps small operators plan with fewer unknowns.', false, false, '2027-03-06', '2027-03-06', 2, '12:45:00', '14:45:00', 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Two-day gathering: Minister Sheila Malcolmson summarized SDPR actions in Sunshine Coast, with partners like Service BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 3, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 22, 29, 1, 1, 1, '2025-08-27 21:43:51-08', '2026-02-16 15:01:24-08', 1),
  (90, 'TACS-000090', 'Minister Anne Kang announced destination development funding, film incentives and sport event sup...', 23, NULL, 'FYI ONLY: Minister Anne Kang announced destination development funding, film incentives and sport event support in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), working with Destination BC and Creative BC to extend shoulder-season visits. Investments will improve accessibility, trail networks and cultural spaces in collaboration with local nations. Regional stakeholders from Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Why people care: Accessible trails and cultural spaces broaden who gets to enjoy B.C., residents first. Events bring visitors, but also community pride and volunteer energy. It’s incremental, but tangible.', true, false, '2027-05-28', '2027-05-28', 2, '10:00:00', '13:00:00', 2, 'Embargoed until 09:00 PT on release day. Virtual technical briefing the day before.', NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Fyi only: Minister Anne Kang summarized TACS actions in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), with partners like Destination BC. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 3, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 23, 30, 3, 1, 1, '2025-04-04 17:01:58-08', '2026-02-17 14:58:08-08', 1),
  (91, 'MOTT-000091', 'Minister Mike Farnworth outlined near-term upgrades to Highway 1 and transit hubs, including new ...', 24, NULL, 'FYI ONLY: Minister Mike Farnworth outlined near-term upgrades to Highway 1 and transit hubs, including new bus priority lanes in North Shore, while continuing work with TransLink and BC Transit on ridership recovery and with BC Ferries on sailing reliability. The update included construction milestones for active transportation links and integrated fare pilots to simplify inter-regional travel. Regional stakeholders from North Shore will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Better ferry/transit alignment eases weekend bottlenecks and helps shift workers make early runs without costly detours. People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days. It supports local hiring and keeps dollars circulating here.', false, false, '2027-03-30', '2027-03-30', 2, '10:15:00', '13:15:00', 2, 'Rolling announcement series; this stop follows Prince George and precedes Kelowna.', NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, 'Fyi only: Minister Mike Farnworth summarized MOTI actions in North Shore, with partners like TransLink. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation. The update aligns with government priorities and reinforces collaboration across ministries and Indigenous partners.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 24, 31, 3, 1, 1, '2025-06-21 04:55:29-08', '2026-01-27 00:05:41-08', 1),
  (92, 'WLRS-000092', 'Minister Randene Neill outlined watershed security actions in Langley, integrating habitat restor...', 25, NULL, 'STAKEHOLDER CALL: Minister Randene Neill outlined watershed security actions in Langley, integrating habitat restoration with Living Lakes Canada and expanded data-sharing to support permitting and drought response. The plan strengthens cumulative effects management and inter-ministry coordination. Regional stakeholders from Langley will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'Here’s the significance: Better data and permitting clarity speed up habitat fixes. Less paperwork, clearer timelines, fewer surprises.', false, false, NULL, NULL, 2, '11:15:00', '13:15:00', 2, 'Targeting late Q1; coordinating venues with local partners. Media advisory to follow.', NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Stakeholder call: Minister Randene Neill summarized WLRS actions in Langley, with partners like BC Parks. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 25, 32, 1, 1, 1, '2025-09-06 06:29:20-08', '2026-02-21 15:24:45-08', 1),
  (93, 'AF-000093', 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Lana Popham provided an update relevant to Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), with i...', 2, NULL, 'OPEN HOUSE: Minister Lana Popham provided an update relevant to Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), with initiatives connected to the AF mandate and partners like BC Milk Marketing Board, Investment Agriculture Foundation, BC Farmers'' Markets. Regional stakeholders from Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'People see quicker, clearer service and fewer hoops to jump through–useful on busy days. That means time back in people’s days and money kept in local pockets.', false, false, '2027-02-16', '2027-02-16', 2, '13:45:00', '15:45:00', 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, 'Open house: Minister Lana Popham summarized AF actions in Skeena (Terrace, Kitimat), with partners like BC Milk Marketing Board. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 3, NULL, NULL, 'team', 2, 9, 4, 1, 1, '2025-01-14 08:53:05-08', '2025-08-18 08:48:53-08', 1),
  (94, 'AG-000094', 'Attorney General Niki Sharma introduced measures to streamline the Civil Resolution Tribunal and ...', 3, NULL, 'FYI ONLY: Attorney General Niki Sharma introduced measures to streamline the Civil Resolution Tribunal and bolster resources for the BC Prosecution Service, reducing delays while improving victim services coordination in Victoria. Reforms include digital filing pilots and cross-agency protocols with public safety partners to tackle repeat violent offending. Regional stakeholders from Victoria will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Here’s the significance: Digital filing and data–sharing cut backlogs so serious cases move quicker. Clearer pathways help people self–resolve disputes without costly court time.', false, true, '2027-12-19', '2027-12-19', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Embargoed until 09:00 PT on release day. Virtual technical briefing the day before.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Fyi only: Minister Niki Sharma summarized AG actions in Victoria, with partners like BC Prosecution Service. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 3, 10, 5, 1, 1, '2025-01-04 02:49:41-08', '2025-12-03 01:22:14-08', 1),
  (95, 'MCFD-000095', 'Minister Jodie Wickens announced expanded supports for youth in care and children and youth with ...', 4, NULL, 'TWO-DAY GATHERING: Minister Jodie Wickens announced expanded supports for youth in care and children and youth with support needs in Sooke and West Shore, co-designed with Indigenous partners and community agencies. The initiative strengthens culturally safe services and transitions to adulthood with housing and education pathways. Regional stakeholders from Sooke and West Shore will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'Stability for caregivers and better navigation reduce crisis cycling. Expanded CYWSN and youth–in–care supports close service gaps and ease transitions to housing, work and school.', false, true, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Week of next full moon–exact date pending room availability in community hall.', NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Two-day gathering: Minister Jodie Wickens summarized CFD actions in Sooke and West Shore, with partners like BCGEU. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 4, 11, 4, 1, 1, '2025-10-14 06:53:01-08', '2026-02-18 10:25:33-08', 1),
  (96, 'CITZ-000096', 'Minister Diana Gibson announced a digital service refresh for Service BC locations in Sunshine Co...', 5, NULL, 'THIRD-PARTY EVENT: Minister Diana Gibson announced a digital service refresh for Service BC locations in Sunshine Coast, expanding identity verification, permitting portals and connectivity with the BCDevExchange community. The work advances secure-by-design standards and plain-language service improvements across channels. Regional stakeholders from Sunshine Coast will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce. The ministry emphasized transparency, data publication and measurable milestones, with quarterly reporting.', 'From a resident’s view: Plain–language, secure–by–design services make government simpler and safer to use. More predictability; better service; safer communities.', true, true, '2027-06-08', '2027-06-08', 1, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, 7, NULL, NULL, 'Third-party event: Minister Diana Gibson summarized CITZ actions in Sunshine Coast, with partners like BC Registries. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'reviewed', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'team', 5, 12, 3, 1, 1, '2025-05-03 06:29:44-08', '2026-02-16 15:42:07-08', 1),
  (97, 'ECC-000097', 'Minister Lisa Beare outlined new classroom additions and early learning spaces in Okanagan (Kelow...', 6, NULL, 'COMMUNITY ROUNDTABLE: Minister Lisa Beare outlined new classroom additions and early learning spaces in Okanagan (Kelowna, Vernon, Penticton), coordinated with school districts and BCTF to support enrolment growth and workforce needs. Funding also supports seismic upgrades and inclusive education resources developed with local educators. Regional stakeholders from Okanagan (Kelowna, Vernon, Penticton) will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'If you live here: Seismic upgrades protect students and staff–peace of mind for families. Better supports for inclusive education mean more kids can thrive close to home. Less red tape and more coordination make it easier to plan ahead.', false, true, '2027-06-29', '2027-06-29', 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Tentative: first week of next month, subject to travel windows and weather.', NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, 'Community roundtable: Minister Lisa Beare summarized ECC actions in Okanagan (Kelowna, Vernon, Penticton), with partners like BC School Trustees Association. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 6, 13, 4, 1, 1, '2025-04-18 19:47:45-08', '2026-02-23 03:56:55-08', 1),
  (98, 'EMCR-000098', 'Minister Kelly Greene detailed seasonal preparedness for floods, drought and wildfire in Cowichan...', 7, NULL, 'JOINT ANNOUNCEMENT: Minister Kelly Greene detailed seasonal preparedness for floods, drought and wildfire in Cowichan Valley, highlighting resources from PreparedBC and EmergencyInfoBC and community-level evacuation planning. Investments include modernized emergency operations centres and enhanced public alerting with local authorities. Regional stakeholders from Cowichan Valley will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'For businesses: PreparedBC resources make it easier for families to build kits and plans they’ll actually use. Co–ordinated planning reduces overlap and confusion between agencies on bad days. Less red tape and more coordination make it easier to plan ahead. It’s incremental, but tangible.', false, false, '2026-12-06', '2026-12-06', 2, '16:00:00', '17:00:00', 2, 'Rolling announcement series; this stop follows Prince George and precedes Kelowna.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Joint announcement: Minister Kelly Greene summarized EMCR actions in Cowichan Valley, with partners like BC Wildfire Service. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'events', false, NULL, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 7, 14, 3, 1, 1, '2024-10-23 09:06:37-08', '2026-03-01 11:17:06-08', 1),
  (99, 'ECS-000099', 'Minister Adrian Dix outlined grid-scale investments with BC Hydro and industrial electrification ...', 8, NULL, 'TWO-DAY GATHERING: Minister Adrian Dix outlined grid-scale investments with BC Hydro and industrial electrification opportunities in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky, advancing CleanBC goals and supporting new critical-minerals processing. The plan includes fast-tracked interconnections for future projects and expanded heat-pump incentives for homes and small businesses. Regional stakeholders from Whistler and Sea-to-Sky will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'In a nutshell: Grid upgrades and electrification cut industrial emissions and create skilled jobs in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky. Faster interconnections mean clean projects come online sooner, reducing energy costs over time.', true, true, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, NULL, 2, 'Rolling announcement series; this stop follows Prince George and precedes Kelowna.', NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, 'Two-day gathering: Minister Adrian Dix summarized ECS actions in Whistler and Sea-to-Sky, with partners like BC Hydro. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'new', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 3, NULL, NULL, 'team', 8, 15, 3, 1, 1, '2025-03-12 12:25:45-08', '2026-02-22 08:49:03-08', 1),
  (100, 'EP-000100', 'Minister Tamara Davidson announced expanded conservation investments and trail upgrades in Sooke ...', 9, NULL, 'BUDGET BACKGROUNDER: Minister Tamara Davidson announced expanded conservation investments and trail upgrades in Sooke and West Shore, with BC Parks and the Conservation Officer Service enhancing access while supporting habitat and climate resilience. The ministry also highlighted permitting efficiencies through the Environmental Assessment Office for clean-economy projects. Regional stakeholders from Sooke and West Shore will join the discussion, including local governments and Chambers of Commerce.', 'In practical terms: Upgraded trails and habitat work in Sooke and West Shore balance access and conservation–good for residents, tourism and wildlife. The changes are small on paper but add up across a year of errands, commitments and bills. That means time back in people’s days and money kept in local pockets.', true, false, NULL, NULL, 2, '15:15:00', '17:00:00', 2, 'Date TBD; aiming to align with regional council schedule. Minister''s Office approved.', NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, 'Budget backgrounder: Minister Tamara Davidson summarized EP actions in Sooke and West Shore, with partners like BC Parks. Focus is on near-term delivery, measurable milestones and clear benefits for communities. Stakeholder input will shape final details before implementation.', 'changed', 'issues', false, NULL, NULL, 1, 2, NULL, NULL, 'global', 9, 16, 4, 1, 1, '2024-12-27 20:15:06-08', '2026-02-26 06:56:41-08', 1)

